1. Monolith application:
Flipkart Project
   1. Login Page/Authentication.
   2. Products catalog
   3  Payment Processing
   4. Order management.
   5. All UI also in same codebase.

  The monolith application will be easy during initial development or for POCS.

 In Monolith Architecture
     - All features are tightly integrated and work as one large system. 
     - Lets say there is issue in Product catalog page/Payment processing page/Order management page, 
     the whole application will go down or crash.
     - Small change in one module is deployed, the testing needs to be done for whole app.
     - Its very difficcult to introduce new feature safely, bcz change in one module may effect other modules too. 
     - You must scale entire application, not just part i need. - scalability issue. 
     - Slower Development - 
          Products catalog - changes that can be done in 3 to 4 days. ()
          Payment Processing - International payments acceptance - very big chnage - 2 months.
          Order management. - One month.
         All has to go for production at a time, so the development process is very slow.
     - Technology Lockin
         EX: Products catalog - This can be done more feasible and effectively written using python
         Order Management - using PHP can be done better.
         Tech upgrade for each module is not possible with Monolith architecture.
      Difficult to maintain.
        - Code base becomes huge and complex.
        - New developers takes long time to understand.     


Microservices Architecture:
----------------------------
In Microservice Architecture, we break entire system into small independent services.

Flipkart
   1. Login Page/Authentication. - Service - spring boot app
   2. Products catalog - service - spring boot app
   3. Payment Processing - service - spring boot app
   4. Order management. - service - spring boot app
   5. All UI also in same codebase. (angular app)

1) Monolith Problem : If one module fails, whole app goes down.
  Microservice Fix: fault isolation(Only the service that went wrong goes down, the entire still be working.)

2) Problem: Small change in one module is deployed, the testing needs to be done for whole app.
   Microservice Fix: Independent deployment.
   EX: change in product catalog, deploy only that service. 
   you dont need to deploy all other services

3) Problem: Hard To introdcuce New feature:
    Microservice Fix: Service Isolation
    If there is new feature has to be added in order service, do that feature for order service
    and deploy only that service.

4) Scalability issue. We need to increase the memory of whole system   
    Microservice Fix: Independent scaling
    EX: If Products catalog service is most businest service then we allocate max. memory to this service.
    Rest of the services can use nominal memory.

5) Problem:  Slower Development 
          Products catalog - changes that can be done in 3 to 4 days. ()
          Payment Processing - International payments acceptance - very big chnage - 2 months.
          Order management. - One month.
  microservice Fix: Parallel development and release process.
  Products catalog  - development done in 3 to 4 days, testing 3 day , deployment.
  Payment Processing - International payments acceptance - very big chnage - 2 months. + 1 month testing -> release 
  
6) Problem:  Technology Lock in:
   Microservice Fix:  Polyglot architecture - Its a design approach where a system utililizes multiple programming languages, frameworks codebases within same ecosystem.
   This makes us select best tool for specific problem.
   EX: Products catalog  - Python
    Payment Processing - PHP
    Order Mnagaement - Java.

7) Problem:  Difficult to maintain(huge codebases)    
  Microservice Fix: Smaller codebases
  Each service is small and focused
  Easier for new developer.

